WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:23.090
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:23.360 --> 00:30.320
♪ Even though my heart says I love you ♪

3
00:30.320 --> 00:35.560
♪ Why am I like this? ♪

4
00:35.560 --> 00:38.320
♪ I don't understand ♪

5
00:38.320 --> 00:43.720
♪ What's wrong with my mouth and my heart? ♪

6
00:43.720 --> 00:48.920
♪ Why won't they say the same thing? ♪

7
00:48.920 --> 00:55.080
♪ Will we ever get to love each other? ♪

8
00:57.040 --> 01:00.680
Since Parn started seeing you, she hasn't been working here anymore.

9
01:00.960 --> 01:02.320
But she's still accepting clients.

10
01:02.320 --> 01:04.200
Sis Mol owed ten million to a loan shark.

11
01:04.200 --> 01:06.480
She came to help, so they wouldn't take over this place.

12
01:06.720 --> 01:09.200
If you love Peem, let her go.

13
01:10.200 --> 01:12.520
Didn't she tell you that I'm gay?

14
01:13.080 --> 01:14.440
You misunderstood Parn.

15
01:15.080 --> 01:17.800
Get yourself together before it's too late

16
01:17.800 --> 01:19.240
to win her back.

17
01:19.760 --> 01:20.800
Opening day.

18
01:26.200 --> 01:27.280
Hey.

19
01:27.960 --> 01:29.440
Do you think I should tell her?

20
01:32.680 --> 01:34.320
I don't think you should.

21
01:34.759 --> 01:36.160
It's good that she's moved on.

22
01:37.240 --> 01:39.800
Plus, today is a good day.

23
01:40.240 --> 01:42.200
If you bring that up, it'll ruin the mood.

24
01:42.560 --> 01:43.479
You're right.

25
01:44.039 --> 01:45.120
- Let's go. - Let's go.

26
01:48.680 --> 01:49.640
How long have you been here?

27
01:51.120 --> 01:53.600
- Parn! - Miew! Pat!

28
01:55.320 --> 01:57.120
Sis isn't coming. She can't.

29
01:57.120 --> 01:59.240
It's okay. So that's why I haven't seen her.

30
01:59.240 --> 02:01.880
Someone is courting her.

31
02:02.160 --> 02:03.280
He's rich too.

32
02:04.000 --> 02:04.800
Who is it?

33
02:05.840 --> 02:06.880
It's Tot.

34
02:07.080 --> 02:08.639
Huh? Really?

35
02:08.919 --> 02:09.880
- Yes. - Yes.

36
02:12.320 --> 02:15.160
- Alright, let's give her our well wishes. - Yeah, yeah, yeah.

37
02:15.160 --> 02:16.400
But let me go first.

38
02:16.400 --> 02:17.560
Sure.

39
02:18.360 --> 02:20.440
Here you go!

40
02:21.000 --> 02:27.280
Ahem! I wish for your shop to become a massive success!

41
02:27.280 --> 02:30.120
Let your success ring around the world!

42
02:30.120 --> 02:32.000
I hope you make a big profit.

43
02:32.000 --> 02:35.640
Whatever you're selling, I hope it sells like it's free.

44
02:36.600 --> 02:40.079
May you get so rich,

45
02:40.079 --> 02:43.560
you'll beg for it to stop!

46
02:43.560 --> 02:46.040
Ridiculously rich!

47
02:46.040 --> 02:47.320
Sadhu!

48
02:48.000 --> 02:49.040
Here.

49
02:51.040 --> 02:53.600
It's lucky money.

50
02:55.280 --> 02:56.640
Yeah, take it.

51
02:56.640 --> 02:58.079
Thank you.

52
03:05.520 --> 03:10.120
I knew it! My gaydar was beeping so hard.

53
03:13.120 --> 03:15.240
Techin also left me the bakery's business card.

54
03:15.520 --> 03:16.400
Oh my.

55
03:17.240 --> 03:18.640
What a nice guy.

56
03:18.640 --> 03:20.560
Did he leave his card for me too?

57
03:23.920 --> 03:25.000
So no.

58
03:25.320 --> 03:26.440
Fine, keep going.

59
03:28.360 --> 03:30.640
Parn only accepts jobs that involve serving drinks and drinking with clients,

60
03:30.640 --> 03:31.680
but she won't sleep with them.

61
03:31.960 --> 03:35.640
As for meal dates, she only goes with those she already knows and trusts.

62
03:35.640 --> 03:36.840
Mm.

63
03:36.840 --> 03:40.760
That means Parn had never slept with her clients.

64
03:42.600 --> 03:44.079
She said I was the first.

65
03:44.440 --> 03:47.280
Well, I guess it's true.

66
03:52.360 --> 03:54.800
How will she ever repay five million to me?

67
03:54.800 --> 03:56.720
How long will running a bakery take to pay off the debt?

68
03:57.680 --> 03:58.960
And now you're worried about her?

69
03:59.400 --> 04:02.920
Turns out you've misunderstood her all this time, about everything.

70
04:03.360 --> 04:04.360
Yeah.

71
04:04.800 --> 04:05.960
What are you going to do next?

72
04:07.840 --> 04:08.960
Ugh!

73
04:09.440 --> 04:11.560
I really thought she was deceiving me.

74
04:12.440 --> 04:13.560
Stop it.

75
04:13.560 --> 04:15.880
Stop trying to justify your thoughts.

76
04:16.079 --> 04:19.519
Right now, you need to figure out what you're going to do.

77
04:22.040 --> 04:22.760
So?

78
04:28.360 --> 04:29.320
You love her.

79
04:31.640 --> 04:32.520
Yeah.

80
04:33.120 --> 04:34.840
And very much too.

81
04:35.520 --> 04:36.320
I do.

82
04:39.400 --> 04:40.760
Go make up with her then.

83
04:41.320 --> 04:43.000
- I do want to. - Oh?

84
04:44.159 --> 04:46.000
- Hey! - Don't "hey" me.

85
04:46.000 --> 04:48.800
Go make up with her if you want to. Why stay stubborn?

86
04:49.240 --> 04:51.800
If you love her, there's no need for any reasons.

87
04:52.000 --> 04:54.080
Go patch things up with her. Just go.

88
04:54.760 --> 04:56.760
It's not that simple.

89
04:56.760 --> 04:58.520
I put her through quite a lot.

90
04:58.880 --> 05:00.920
If you put her through a lot,

91
05:00.920 --> 05:03.480
put just as much effort into winning her back.

92
05:03.920 --> 05:05.760
But she put me through a lot too.

93
05:05.760 --> 05:07.520
Why did she have to lie to me?

94
05:07.520 --> 05:09.640
If she'd told me, I'd have been happy to help.

95
05:11.880 --> 05:13.160
Then just forget it.

96
05:13.160 --> 05:14.200
Let her go.

97
05:14.200 --> 05:15.840
That way, you can also meet someone new.

98
05:15.840 --> 05:18.640
Whatever you gave her, just think of it as a gesture of affection.

99
05:18.920 --> 05:20.640
It won't put a dent in your bank account, right?

100
05:21.280 --> 05:22.640
More importantly,

101
05:23.520 --> 05:28.360
hatred is never appeased by hatred.

102
05:30.080 --> 05:34.320
Whatever wrong she's done to you, let karma take its course.

103
05:36.280 --> 05:38.480
And why do I have to let her go so easily?

104
05:38.480 --> 05:41.000
She hurt me. Does she think she can live a good life now?

105
05:41.640 --> 05:43.520
Since karma isn't fast enough,

106
05:43.520 --> 05:45.840
Parn will have to face me.

107
05:46.960 --> 05:47.960
Huh?

108
05:56.320 --> 05:58.320
Whoa!

109
05:59.360 --> 06:00.880
Parn!

110
06:01.280 --> 06:02.680
Please come in.

111
06:03.960 --> 06:05.240
Please come in.

112
06:08.520 --> 06:10.800
Pan Pas...

113
06:15.640 --> 06:17.120
Pan Pastry-ne!

114
06:17.680 --> 06:19.040
What's with the name?

115
06:22.840 --> 06:24.360
Parn and Phakanee?

116
06:27.360 --> 06:28.360
Yeah.

117
06:31.320 --> 06:34.840
You used her money to open a shop, so you named it after her?

118
06:35.680 --> 06:36.680
Are you crazy?

119
06:44.040 --> 06:45.120
Hey!

120
06:45.120 --> 06:47.240
- First order! - First order!

121
06:51.240 --> 06:56.200
Hey, wait. Ding, ding, ding...

122
06:56.200 --> 06:57.200
Whoa!

123
06:58.960 --> 06:59.960
Is the machine broken?

124
07:00.560 --> 07:01.960
The orders keep coming in.

125
07:01.960 --> 07:02.960
Isn't it good?

126
07:07.320 --> 07:08.760
Oh...

127
07:09.600 --> 07:11.240
Let's close the shop.

128
07:12.920 --> 07:16.240
Yeah, before my body shuts down.

129
07:21.640 --> 07:22.720
Hey.

130
07:23.680 --> 07:27.360
If I'd known a bakery would sell this well,

131
07:27.840 --> 07:29.880
I wouldn't be working at the club.

132
07:30.520 --> 07:32.240
Come on, Miew.

133
07:34.240 --> 07:36.080
That means they must taste good.

134
07:36.440 --> 07:38.520
You can't even fry an egg without burning it.

135
07:38.520 --> 07:39.800
And you think you can bake?

136
07:40.800 --> 07:42.240
Pat! Ugh!

137
07:42.880 --> 07:44.120
Come on, you two.

138
07:45.440 --> 07:48.080
- Jeez! - Jeez, you still haven't turned it off?

139
07:48.080 --> 07:50.720
Oh, no.

140
07:50.720 --> 07:55.159
I can't go on. My hands are shaking.

141
07:57.920 --> 07:59.080
I'll give you a massage.

142
08:03.120 --> 08:05.560
Seriously? She's still accepting orders?

143
08:08.440 --> 08:09.400
There's nothing here.

144
08:09.920 --> 08:10.920
Huh?

145
08:12.920 --> 08:14.120
Oh, right.

146
08:15.560 --> 08:18.520
It's my phone. Sis texted me.

147
08:18.520 --> 08:20.200
- Ugh! - Ugh!

148
08:20.200 --> 08:21.560
Sorry.

149
08:22.520 --> 08:25.920
If one more order comes in, I'll drop dead here.

150
08:26.480 --> 08:28.840
When the delivery driver gets here, just let them take me instead.

151
08:29.080 --> 08:30.440
Straight to the temple.

152
08:31.640 --> 08:34.520
- Kusala Dhamma... - Quit it.

153
08:34.799 --> 08:36.039
It's a good day today.

154
08:36.440 --> 08:38.440
- I forgot. - I can't believe you two.

155
08:39.520 --> 08:41.840
It's true that you got a lot of orders,

156
08:41.840 --> 08:44.240
but when I was sorting them, I only saw one name.

157
08:45.080 --> 08:46.320
- Really? - Yeah.

158
08:46.320 --> 08:49.360
Won't they get diabetes at this rate?

159
08:50.040 --> 08:50.760
Right.

160
08:50.760 --> 08:53.600
I was so busy getting the orders ready I didn't notice.

161
08:53.600 --> 08:55.000
Do you remember the name?

162
08:56.360 --> 08:58.680
I think it's Pee...

163
09:00.240 --> 09:01.920
Pee...

164
09:03.800 --> 09:04.680
Peekinak.

165
09:05.400 --> 09:06.440
Peekinak?

166
09:06.720 --> 09:07.760
Mm.

167
09:15.120 --> 09:16.880
She must have died right at the oven.

168
09:19.240 --> 09:20.120
Ms. Peem.

169
09:20.800 --> 09:22.480
What should we do with these?

170
09:23.720 --> 09:26.080
Bring me a box to try. I doubt it'll be any good.

171
09:26.680 --> 09:28.800
Give the rest away to the staff and my friends.

172
10:12.400 --> 10:13.680
The last one.

173
10:20.640 --> 10:21.960
It's so good.

174
10:23.440 --> 10:25.920
The cake isn't too sweet, and it's so smooth. Perfect!

175
10:27.120 --> 10:28.360
It's so good!

176
10:33.200 --> 10:34.960
I'll tire you out even more tomorrow.

177
10:42.360 --> 10:43.360
Okay...

178
11:01.280 --> 11:02.480
So she can still handle it.

179
11:14.560 --> 11:16.320
She got good reviews too.

180
11:21.760 --> 11:23.080
"The pastries are delicious."

181
11:24.560 --> 11:26.240
"The owner is pretty."

182
11:31.720 --> 11:33.280
You drove 30 kilometers for this?

183
11:34.400 --> 11:37.000
Who forced you? Why didn't you buy something nearby?

184
11:37.840 --> 11:39.920
"Just seeing the owner is refreshing."

185
11:40.360 --> 11:42.320
Oh, please. It's a cake shop.

186
12:06.680 --> 12:07.800
Ow!

187
12:13.600 --> 12:14.720
Why don't you get up?

188
12:15.320 --> 12:16.560
Why are you sitting there?

189
12:28.440 --> 12:30.280
Why didn't you tell me Techin is gay?

190
12:39.920 --> 12:40.880
Why didn't you answer me?

191
12:40.880 --> 12:41.960
Didn't you hear me?

192
12:47.520 --> 12:50.000
I heard you, but I didn't want to answer.

193
12:53.080 --> 12:54.400
Will it kill you to answer?

194
12:58.200 --> 13:00.240
You like him because he's rich, don't you?

195
13:00.680 --> 13:02.120
But I'm richer, you know?

196
13:02.120 --> 13:04.360
Plus, he likes guys, not girls like you.

197
13:05.160 --> 13:07.160
What? You want to fix a gay man?

198
13:07.760 --> 13:09.440
Is that even possible?

199
13:10.720 --> 13:12.240
He's gay. It's not like he has a cold.

200
13:13.960 --> 13:15.680
Just like me. I love you.

201
13:16.000 --> 13:18.240
Even if there were 100 other men, I'd still love you.

202
13:19.080 --> 13:20.320
It can't be fixed.

203
13:24.720 --> 13:25.560
Ms. Peem!

204
13:27.560 --> 13:29.040
You have no right to do that to me.

205
13:35.480 --> 13:36.440
Why?

206
13:37.480 --> 13:39.160
So I can't do it unless I pay?

207
13:40.440 --> 13:43.080
Will you stop saying things to hurt my feelings like this?

208
13:44.440 --> 13:46.280
I thought you didn't want to see my face.

209
13:46.720 --> 13:47.800
Why are you here?

210
13:51.160 --> 13:52.600
I'm here to buy these buildings.

211
13:52.920 --> 13:54.440
Then go look at them.

212
13:54.920 --> 13:56.320
Just leave me alone.

213
14:18.320 --> 14:19.600
Hey.

214
14:19.600 --> 14:22.080
You called me here just to ignore me?

215
14:22.080 --> 14:24.240
Am I supposed to talk to the table?

216
14:29.200 --> 14:31.440
Parn said things between us were over.

217
14:31.840 --> 14:33.840
Well, you broke up with her.

218
14:35.080 --> 14:35.920
I did.

219
14:36.120 --> 14:37.920
But it's not my fault, is it?

220
14:37.920 --> 14:40.280
She broke her promise, so I broke up with her.

221
14:40.520 --> 14:43.200
She had a date with Techin and a job at Paradise.

222
14:43.920 --> 14:46.720
But now you know they're not what you thought they were.

223
14:46.720 --> 14:47.680
So what?

224
14:49.320 --> 14:52.160
I told you to patch things up, but you ended up getting slapped.

225
14:52.800 --> 14:54.000
I tried to.

226
14:54.960 --> 14:58.040
By ordering her pastries for the entire country?

227
14:59.200 --> 15:00.080
No.

228
15:00.840 --> 15:02.960
Then why did you do that?

229
15:03.720 --> 15:06.800
I just wanted to work her so hard she'd collapse right there by the oven.

230
15:07.440 --> 15:08.760
Really?

231
15:08.960 --> 15:09.880
Yeah.

232
15:10.640 --> 15:14.800
Or were you just helping her business grow?

233
15:19.880 --> 15:21.480
You're such a Siberian Husky.

234
15:21.920 --> 15:22.920
What do you mean?

235
15:23.360 --> 15:26.320
You're stubborn, self-centered, and bark at everything.

236
15:26.720 --> 15:27.880
You're exaggerating.

237
15:29.480 --> 15:30.760
Yet you do love her.

238
15:34.600 --> 15:36.840
Instead of patching things up, you insulted her.

239
15:37.160 --> 15:38.800
Then you kissed her and got slapped for it.

240
15:38.800 --> 15:40.760
How are you ever going to get back together with her?

241
15:51.000 --> 15:52.000
It's for Ms. Parn.

242
15:58.000 --> 15:59.400
(Parn - From Peem)

243
16:00.080 --> 16:01.080
Wait.

244
16:02.640 --> 16:03.640
Yes?

245
16:06.400 --> 16:07.720
Please return it.

246
16:10.080 --> 16:10.960
Return?

247
16:15.200 --> 16:16.400
Why did she return it?

248
16:16.400 --> 16:17.600
Excuse me, Ms. Peem.

249
16:22.680 --> 16:24.240
I was trying to make up with you.

250
16:34.040 --> 16:35.200
Thank you.

251
16:46.600 --> 16:48.160
Why didn't you accept the flowers?

252
16:49.160 --> 16:51.920
You have the right to send them. I have the right to refuse them.

253
16:56.000 --> 16:56.800
What's wrong with you?

254
16:57.680 --> 16:59.080
I should be asking you.

255
16:59.080 --> 17:01.520
You said you didn't want to see me, but you keep coming.

256
17:01.520 --> 17:03.160
If you're open, you have to serve your customers.

257
17:03.160 --> 17:04.280
I'm a customer, aren't I?

258
17:04.960 --> 17:07.160
We're closed now. We're not accepting any more customers.

259
17:09.079 --> 17:10.560
You're not accepting customers who come for the cakes.

260
17:11.640 --> 17:12.960
But do you still accept customers who want a meal date?

261
17:14.000 --> 17:15.560
Or just those looking for intimacy?

262
17:18.359 --> 17:19.319
Ms. Peem!

263
17:21.440 --> 17:23.440
Stop doing this to me.

264
17:24.359 --> 17:25.839
I'm a human being too.

265
17:30.240 --> 17:31.240
Get out.

266
17:33.520 --> 17:34.760
I said get out!

267
17:45.080 --> 17:47.240
Oh my. Serves you right.

268
17:48.440 --> 17:50.320
I didn't call you here to rub it in.

269
17:50.840 --> 17:52.640
You brought it upon yourself.

270
17:53.000 --> 17:56.680
That wasn't patching things up. You were just being an asshole.

271
18:00.040 --> 18:02.640
I've never had to win anyone back before.

272
18:02.640 --> 18:04.600
I just got angry when she stood up to me.

273
18:05.400 --> 18:06.480
I'm sorry.

274
18:09.800 --> 18:10.880
Why did you apologize to me?

275
18:11.280 --> 18:12.640
Try saying it.

276
18:13.560 --> 18:14.560
Say what?

277
18:14.560 --> 18:16.840
Say you're sorry.

278
18:16.840 --> 18:18.160
"I'm sorry."

279
18:18.360 --> 18:19.480
Are you insane?

280
18:19.480 --> 18:20.920
Why should I apologize to you?

281
18:21.240 --> 18:23.880
It's a practice. So you can say it to Parn.

282
18:25.920 --> 18:28.800
But I guess someone like you doesn't know how to say it.

283
18:32.720 --> 18:35.160
I'm sorry for making you feel bad that night.

284
18:41.160 --> 18:42.240
I've said it before.

285
18:43.000 --> 18:44.200
I know how to do it.

286
18:45.000 --> 18:46.280
Then say it to her.

287
18:46.720 --> 18:50.800
If money can't win her forgiveness, try this.

288
18:51.320 --> 18:53.800
Feelings can't be bought with money.

289
18:54.320 --> 18:55.760
They come from the heart.

290
18:57.920 --> 19:01.680
Gosh. Earlier, you just said, "Parn will have to face me."

291
19:01.680 --> 19:02.680
How did that go, huh?

292
19:07.880 --> 19:09.640
Why do you look so dejected?

293
19:13.600 --> 19:15.560
I've never seen you like this before.

294
19:16.080 --> 19:17.560
Be confident.

295
19:19.840 --> 19:21.760
Just like when you insulted her, yeah?

296
19:22.360 --> 19:24.400
Hey, are you mocking me?

297
19:24.400 --> 19:25.640
No.

298
19:25.640 --> 19:27.080
Just offering some advice.

299
19:27.880 --> 19:29.520
You should be confident.

300
19:29.520 --> 19:33.160
After all, your father is a business tycoon.

301
19:33.160 --> 19:36.080
And you're a third-generation heir to the Traisuvetthiwat family,

302
19:37.160 --> 19:40.920
which owns the biggest shopping mall in Thailand.

303
19:48.080 --> 19:49.120
Hey.

304
19:59.840 --> 20:02.240
Parn, didn't you hear me?

305
20:05.360 --> 20:07.240
Huh? What is it?

306
20:07.680 --> 20:10.040
Jeez.

307
20:10.360 --> 20:11.960
She's been calling you for a while now.

308
20:11.960 --> 20:12.880
Really?

309
20:13.120 --> 20:14.040
- Yes. - Yes.

310
20:15.400 --> 20:16.600
What's wrong?

311
20:17.080 --> 20:19.160
Must be about Ms. Peem, huh?

312
20:20.280 --> 20:21.600
Come on, tell us.

313
20:32.240 --> 20:33.480
Who summoned the Devil?

314
20:33.480 --> 20:34.960
No one did.

315
20:34.960 --> 20:36.040
Let's go.

316
20:40.920 --> 20:43.760
Well, we'll go out to grab a bite.

317
20:43.760 --> 20:44.920
We'll buy something for you too.

318
